WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:21.833 --> 00:00:26.466
[Narrator:] This is the story of the United States 
Public Health Service.

00:00:26.466 --> 00:00:28.966
It's a story of many parts.

00:00:28.966 --> 00:00:35.232
It's a story of hospitals like this one in New Orleans 
and this one in Norfolk, Virginia.

00:00:35.233 --> 00:00:38.766
It's a story of the leprosarium in Carville, Louisiana,

00:00:38.766 --> 00:00:45.099
the hospital for study and treatment of drug 
addiction in Lexington, Kentucky,

00:00:45.100 --> 00:00:51.800
the National Institutes of Health in Bethesda, 
Maryland, and the Clinical Center there.

00:00:53.240 --> 00:00:58.766
It's the story of quarantine stations at our major 
ports of entry like this one at Miami,

00:00:58.766 --> 00:01:01.732
and this one at New Orleans.

00:01:01.733 --> 00:01:06.933
As a matter of fact, the story of the Public Health 
Service can be found in many places

00:01:06.933 --> 00:01:09.733
throughout the United States and its territories.

00:01:09.733 --> 00:01:13.133
[ Music ]

00:01:13.133 --> 00:01:17.666
The story began with President John Adams in 
1798, when he signed the Act

00:01:17.666 --> 00:01:23.966
establishing the  Marine Hospital Service, 
forerunner of the Public Health Service today.

00:01:23.966 --> 00:01:28.032
Many people have helped establish the Service's 
distinguished traditions,

00:01:28.033 --> 00:01:31.833
people like Joseph Goldberger, who pioneered in 
studies of pellagra,

00:01:31.833 --> 00:01:35.633
a once widespread dietary disease.

00:01:35.633 --> 00:01:40.933
Leslie Lumsden, whose work in typhoid 
epidemiology and rural sanitation

00:01:40.940 --> 00:01:44.660
is a cornerstone of modern public health practice.

00:01:45.700 --> 00:01:50.400
Joseph Mountain who stimulated nationwide 
interest in many fields of public health practice

00:01:50.400 --> 00:01:56.000
and administration, such as chronic disease control 
and the health problems of the aging.

00:01:56.440 --> 00:02:03.166
Charles Armstrong whose adaptation of 
poliomyelitis to rodents speeded up polio research,

00:02:03.166 --> 00:02:07.832
and Edward Francis, whose studies of the origin 
and causes of tularemia have done much

00:02:07.840 --> 00:02:10.420
to improve our knowledge of this disease.

00:02:11.466 --> 00:02:16.620
Other Public Health Service scientists developed 
vaccines against Rocky Mountain Spotted Fever

00:02:16.640 --> 00:02:19.760
and typhus, and perfected many others.

00:02:21.260 --> 00:02:27.440
The Service was also instrumental in the virtual 
eradication of malaria in the United States.

00:02:29.440 --> 00:02:32.600
Today, the Public Health Service employs over 
21,000 people

00:02:32.600 --> 00:02:36.733
in about 250 occupational specialties.

00:02:36.733 --> 00:02:38.633
These include physicians,

00:02:38.640 --> 00:02:39.600
nurses,

00:02:40.166 --> 00:02:41.680
sanitary engineers,

00:02:42.400 --> 00:02:44.120
dentists,

00:02:44.840 --> 00:02:46.440
scientists,

00:02:47.240 --> 00:02:48.780
dieticians,

00:02:49.660 --> 00:02:51.880
veterinarians,

00:02:52.260 --> 00:02:53.820
physical therapists,

00:02:54.140 --> 00:02:55.820
pharmacists,

00:02:56.460 --> 00:02:58.700
social workers,

00:02:59.260 --> 00:03:01.140
administrative specialists,

00:03:01.500 --> 00:03:03.600
instrument-makers,

00:03:03.840 --> 00:03:05.960
animal caretakers,

00:03:06.240 --> 00:03:08.280
nursing assistants,

00:03:08.800 --> 00:03:11.200
clerical personnel,

00:03:11.700 --> 00:03:16.820
and a host of other specialists necessary to the 
effective operation of the Service.

00:03:18.760 --> 00:03:23.380
Civil Service personnel comprise the largest 
number of these employees.

00:03:23.640 --> 00:03:29.700
About one-fifth of the Service's employees are 
regular and reserve officers of the Commissioned 
Corp,

00:03:29.700 --> 00:03:34.633
a long-established career organization of 
professional medical and health personnel,

00:03:34.633 --> 00:03:37.833
and one of the uniformed services of our country.

00:03:37.833 --> 00:03:41.566
Because of the professional nature of the 
Service's activities,

00:03:41.566 --> 00:03:45.632
many of its major programs are directed by 
commissioned officers.

00:03:45.633 --> 00:03:50.566
Officers of the Commissioned Corp serve either in 
the regular corps, or career service,

00:03:50.566 --> 00:03:54.866
or in the reserve corps on active or inactive duty.

00:03:54.866 --> 00:03:58.766
Officers on inactive duty belong to a component of 
the reserve corps

00:03:58.766 --> 00:04:01.580
known as the Commissioned Reserve.

00:04:02.200 --> 00:04:09.133
The Commissioned Reserve is a readily available 
personnel held in reserve for grave national 
emergencies,

00:04:09.140 --> 00:04:15.420
and trained to meet critical situations affecting the 
health and well-being of large numbers of people.

00:04:16.600 --> 00:04:21.000
Such emergencies might involve the destruction of 
our cities,

00:04:21.740 --> 00:04:25.020
extensive illness and death from disease 
epidemics,

00:04:25.020 --> 00:04:30.800
or the unusual health problems associated with 
major natural disasters.

00:04:30.800 --> 00:04:35.800
The Public Health Service is the oldest and largest 
of the five operating agencies that comprise

00:04:35.800 --> 00:04:40.260
the United States Department of Health, Education, 
and Welfare.

00:04:41.200 --> 00:04:46.433
The Public Health Service is organized to work 
closely with state and national organizations

00:04:46.440 --> 00:04:50.280
through national conferences and advisory groups 
of private citizens,

00:04:50.280 --> 00:04:55.660
to give meaning and direction to its many 
programs.

00:04:55.660 --> 00:05:00.320
The actual work of the Service is carried on by four 
major bureaus.

00:05:01.340 --> 00:05:04.966
One of these bureaus is the Office of the Surgeon 
General.

00:05:04.966 --> 00:05:09.900
This is not an operating bureau, but is responsible 
for coordinating activities

00:05:09.900 --> 00:05:14.800
and providing administrative services for the three 
other bureaus.

00:05:14.800 --> 00:05:20.666
The three other bureaus, known as operating 
bureaus, are the Bureau of Medical Services,

00:05:20.666 --> 00:05:25.266
the Bureau of State Services, and the National 
Institutes of Health.

00:05:25.266 --> 00:05:28.840
Let's examine these bureaus and their activities 
one at a time.

00:05:30.340 --> 00:05:33.633
First, the Bureau of Medical Services.

00:05:33.633 --> 00:05:37.033
This bureau operates foreign quarantine programs.

00:05:37.033 --> 00:05:43.066
It administers grants for construction of hospitals 
and medical facilities, operates numerous hospitals

00:05:43.066 --> 00:05:46.932
and outpatient clinics, and the Indian Health 
Program.

00:05:46.933 --> 00:05:50.566
It conducts dental and nursing studies of 
personnel needs,

00:05:50.566 --> 00:05:56.032
and makes professional personnel available upon 
request to other federal agencies.

00:05:56.033 --> 00:06:00.433
Personnel in the Bureau of Medical Services work 
in Public Health Service hospitals

00:06:00.440 --> 00:06:06.480
from Massachusetts to California, and in outpatient 
clinics providing medical care to seamen

00:06:06.500 --> 00:06:11.140
of the United States Merchant Marine, the United  States Coast Guard,

00:06:11.280 --> 00:06:16.333
and the families of Coast Guard officers and enlisted personnel.

00:06:16.340 --> 00:06:21.600
They serve in Public Health Service hospitals and clinics on Indian reservations in the United States and Alaska,

00:06:21.600 --> 00:06:25.200
in federal prisons,

00:06:25.740 --> 00:06:28.580
with the Coast Guard in Alaska,

00:06:28.860 --> 00:06:31.740
and with the Coast Guard on the high seas.

00:06:32.400 --> 00:06:36.700
Personnel from the Bureau of Medical Services are 
also assigned to quarantine duty

00:06:36.700 --> 00:06:40.040
with United States embassies in foreign countries.

00:06:40.600 --> 00:06:45.460
In this country, quarantined personnel are on duty 
at our major seaports,

00:06:45.466 --> 00:06:50.299
and at our international airports, where they 
determine the health status of passengers

00:06:50.300 --> 00:06:53.733
entering the United States from abroad

00:06:53.740 --> 00:06:59.380
and keep daily surveillance for disease-bearing 
insects that may find their way into this country.

00:07:00.600 --> 00:07:05.033
The Bureau of Medical Services is also 
responsible for the Hospital Construction Program,

00:07:05.040 --> 00:07:11.320
under which the federal government matches state 
and local funds for the construction of hospitals

00:07:11.320 --> 00:07:15.920
and other medical facilities in communities where 
there are no such facilities,

00:07:15.940 --> 00:07:19.440
or where existing facilities are inadequate.

00:07:19.940 --> 00:07:25.820
Public Health Practice, the control of disease in the 
community as a whole, is the responsibility of the

00:07:25.833 --> 00:07:30.366
second major operating bureau, the Bureau of 
State Services.

00:07:30.366 --> 00:07:36.332
Through research, demonstration, training, and 
consultation, the personnel of this bureau

00:07:36.340 --> 00:07:41.600
work closely with state and local health agencies 
on many different health problems.

00:07:43.200 --> 00:07:47.240
The bureau coordinates the activities of regional 
staffs located in eight of the

00:07:47.240 --> 00:07:51.400
nine regional headquarters of the Department of 
Health, Education, and Welfare.

00:07:51.400 --> 00:07:56.366
It is through these regional staffs that many of the 
Public Health Service's cooperative federal, state,

00:07:56.366 --> 00:08:00.100
and interstate programs reach the people of this 
country.

00:08:01.440 --> 00:08:06.440
The Bureau of State Services assists state and 
community health officials on such problems

00:08:06.466 --> 00:08:09.066
as mosquito and fly control,

00:08:09.066 --> 00:08:11.466
animal-borne diseases,

00:08:11.466 --> 00:08:14.299
safety of public water supplies,

00:08:14.300 --> 00:08:16.500
water pollution control,

00:08:16.500 --> 00:08:22.280
standards of sanitation governing the preparation 
and serving of food and milk.

00:08:22.966 --> 00:08:27.000
Personnel of the Bureau of State Services study, 
develop, and demonstrate

00:08:27.000 --> 00:08:29.800
methods of community refuse disposal.

00:08:29.800 --> 00:08:35.366
They train local health personnel in effective 
methods of sewage treatment,

00:08:35.366 --> 00:08:40.899
in rodent control, and in housing hygiene.

00:08:40.900 --> 00:08:45.966
They study the relationship between air quality and 
community health

00:08:45.966 --> 00:08:50.780
and conduct research to improve the working 
environment of the industrial worker.

00:08:51.160 --> 00:08:57.060
They also work on Indian reservations to eliminate 
health problems caused by insanitary conditions.

00:08:57.480 --> 00:09:03.080
The Bureau of State Services provides grants to 
states to help them finance health programs,

00:09:03.100 --> 00:09:07.233
such as the establishment of new county and local 
health services.

00:09:07.240 --> 00:09:12.060
In addition, there are grants to states for specific 
health problems.

00:09:12.900 --> 00:09:21.900
These include tuberculosis, diabetes, heart 
disease, venereal disease, cancer,

00:09:21.900 --> 00:09:24.640
and dental decay.

00:09:25.300 --> 00:09:29.760
Grants are also made to support studies of the 
special problems of the older citizens

00:09:29.760 --> 00:09:32.380
in our communities.

00:09:33.500 --> 00:09:39.420
Specially trained epidemic intelligence officers of the Bureau of State Services provide disaster aid

00:09:39.420 --> 00:09:44.340
to states in the form of prompt investigation of 
disease outbreaks.

00:09:44.740 --> 00:09:50.900
Another unit of this bureau, The National Office of 
Vital Statistics, compiles, analyzes, and publishes

00:09:50.900 --> 00:09:56.700
national reports on births, deaths, and disease 
outbreaks.

00:09:56.700 --> 00:10:00.400
To augment its field activities and the research 
programs of the service,

00:10:00.400 --> 00:10:05.940
the Bureau of State Services operates the 
Communicable Disease Center in Atlanta, Georgia,

00:10:05.940 --> 00:10:10.860
the Robert A. Taft Sanitary Engineering Center in 
Cincinnati, Ohio,

00:10:10.860 --> 00:10:15.100
and the Arctic Health Research Center in 
Anchorage, Alaska.

00:10:15.600 --> 00:10:20.760
The global scope of the bureau's activities is 
indicated by its international health programs

00:10:20.766 --> 00:10:26.132
in approximately 60 foreign countries where the 
service provides technical assistance

00:10:26.140 --> 00:10:28.240
in the development of health services.

00:10:30.460 --> 00:10:33.060
Here are some nurses in Iran.

00:10:33.060 --> 00:10:35.940
This is a physician in Formosa

00:10:36.340 --> 00:10:39.533
and this is a sanitary engineer in Iraq.

00:10:39.533 --> 00:10:44.766
The third major operating bureau in the Public 
Health Service is the National Institutes of Health

00:10:44.766 --> 00:10:46.932
in Bethesda, Maryland.

00:10:46.933 --> 00:10:54.733
This bureau referred to for brevity as NIH, consists 
of seven research institutes, a clinical center,

00:10:54.740 --> 00:10:57.920
and four independent divisions.

00:10:58.966 --> 00:11:05.120
Although the service conducts research programs in many places, NIH is the largest installation

00:11:05.140 --> 00:11:07.640
for this type of work.

00:11:09.040 --> 00:11:13.860
In modern, well-equipped laboratories, NIH 
scientists are making important progress

00:11:13.920 --> 00:11:16.660
in many areas of research.

00:11:16.666 --> 00:11:19.166
In areas such as heart disease,

00:11:19.166 --> 00:11:20.932
cancer,

00:11:20.933 --> 00:11:23.266
mental illness,

00:11:23.266 --> 00:11:26.399
arthritis and the metabolic disorders,

00:11:26.400 --> 00:11:29.433
the neurological and sensory disorders,

00:11:29.433 --> 00:11:32.333
allergies and infectious diseases,

00:11:32.333 --> 00:11:35.266
and diseases of the mouth and teeth.

00:11:35.266 --> 00:11:40.299
At the Clinical Center, the findings of the laboratory scientists and the experience of the physician

00:11:40.300 --> 00:11:46.260
are brought together in a concentrated attack on disease to accelerate man's knowledge

00:11:46.260 --> 00:11:51.100
of some of our most stubborn disease problems.

00:11:51.100 --> 00:11:55.440
NIH scientists also work at the Public Health  Service's Rocky Mountain Laboratory

00:11:55.440 --> 00:12:01.080
in Hamilton, Montana, where they study diseases that are transmissible from animals to man.

00:12:01.940 --> 00:12:07.933
NIH has also the responsibility of certifying the  safety, purity and potency of biologics

00:12:07.933 --> 00:12:12.266
used in the treatment of disease.

00:12:12.266 --> 00:12:17.832
Over two-thirds of all the funds appropriated to the National Institutes of Health by the Congress

00:12:17.833 --> 00:12:23.633
are awarded to scientists in the nation's medical schools, universities and other research centers.

00:12:23.633 --> 00:12:27.633
These federal funds are helping to expand medical 
research and research training

00:12:27.633 --> 00:12:29.266
throughout the country.

00:12:29.266 --> 00:12:35.999
As a result, our knowledge of the major diseases 
of man is rapidly increasing, bringing us closer to 
the day

00:12:36.000 --> 00:12:41.433
when the main causes of disability and early death 
can be reduced to a minimum.

00:12:41.433 --> 00:12:47.699
One type of award granted by NIH helps medical 
schools expand their training facilities,

00:12:47.700 --> 00:12:52.466
such as laboratories and classrooms which permit 
modern methods of instruction.

00:12:52.466 --> 00:12:57.066
Another type of award is the Research Fellowship 
which helps talented young scientists

00:12:57.066 --> 00:12:59.732
enter research careers.

00:12:59.740 --> 00:13:03.540
Still other funds are granted to non-profit 
institutions for the construction

00:13:03.540 --> 00:13:08.160
of essential research facilities in many parts of the 
country.

00:13:12.040 --> 00:13:16.966
[Music]

00:13:16.966 --> 00:13:21.999
Now let's look once again, but briefly, at the 
organization of the Public Health Service.

00:13:22.000 --> 00:13:26.600
It is part of the United States Department of Health, 
Education, and Welfare.

00:13:27.340 --> 00:13:32.100
Under the direction of the Surgeon General, the 
Service administers programs

00:13:32.100 --> 00:13:35.100
in three major areas of activity.

00:13:35.100 --> 00:13:38.360
These are research into the causes of disease,

00:13:39.700 --> 00:13:42.760
the prevention of disease and promotion of health,

00:13:44.700 --> 00:13:49.500
and the care and treatment of patients who look to 
us for this kind of service.

00:13:51.640 --> 00:13:57.880
Through its 21,000 employees, the Public Health 
Service today brings benefits to every American,

00:13:58.540 --> 00:14:04.360
not so much as a direct dispenser of services, but 
as a leader and guiding influence.

00:14:06.100 --> 00:14:10.860
The Service's work is reflected in an increasing 
store of professional information,

00:14:10.866 --> 00:14:14.899
[ Music ]

00:14:14.900 --> 00:14:18.433
in popular knowledge of medical developments,

00:14:18.433 --> 00:14:24.333
in improved local health programs throughout the 
United States and its territories.

00:14:24.333 --> 00:14:30.799
The Public Health Service, as it has for more than 
150 years, is dedicating its energies

00:14:30.800 --> 00:14:38.400
and resources to increasing man's knowledge of the cause, prevention, treatment, and control of disease,

00:14:38.400 --> 00:14:42.960
that the people of this nation and their 
children are more adequately protected than

00:14:42.960 --> 00:14:48.200
than ever before from the suffering and hardships  produced by disease.

00:14:48.240 --> 00:14:59.780
[Music

